|~ `::legend`, the kind of the legend of a value, and what is declared
   under it: its print, the print of the value it tells laid out by the
   kind of that value.
   The rules it holds: [QSPRN#legend]. ~|

:legend
  |~~ A legend tells a value: it prints under its tag as the print of the
      value laid out by its kind, `::legend::point[`, each part the kind
      reads by a key or an index on a line of its own beside the gloss of
      its page, so a host prints it as it prints any answer, its comments
      painted as comments, and the text read back is the legend.
      `"~{" | parse !| legend` tells the error at rest of a parse, and
      `payload` answers the value told; a tag name tells the kind it names,
      a comment for each name the kind wires, `::span | legend`.
      ::link~(::any/legend) ::link~(::any/print)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts |~~ The value the legend tells. ~~|
    | proves :printsUnderItsTagAsTheValueItTellsLaidOut
        |~~ A legend prints under its tag as the value it tells laid out, read
            back as the legend.
        ~~|
        ~(::point[0 1 2] | legend | get [~(print | startsWith "::legend::point[") ~(eq (print | parse | answer))] | eq [true true])
    | proves :answersTheValueItTellsByPayload
        |~~ `payload` answers the value a legend tells. ~~|
        ~([1 2] | legend | payload | eq [1 2])

:legend/print
  |~~ Answers the print of the value the legend tells laid out by its kind,
      under the tag of the legend: the head beside the gloss of the page
      `doc` reads of the value, each part its kind reads by a key or an
      index on a line of its own beside the gloss of its page, a part at an
      index named beside it, and every comment closed and whitespace, so
      the text reads back as the legend.
      ::link~(::any/legend)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The print of the value told, laid out. ~~| ::string
    | proves :glossesEachPartItsKindWires
        |~~ A part its kind wires stands beside the gloss of its page and the
            name that reads it.
        ~~|
        ~(::point[0 1 2] | legend | print | lines | get /2 | contains "|~ The line of the point, counted from one · line ~|")
    | impl ::builtin{}
